                DeclarationHandle.Create("D5/S3/VertexAlgebra/Lattice/PhysicalLie/LatticeBRSTCurrentIdentities.b_minus_one_mode"),
                H("The original antighost acts on every integer mode"), StatementSource.WithoutFormula(), AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(),
                Blocks(Paragraph(Text("For every D, original states x,y and integer n, B_(-1)(mu_n(x,y)) = mu_n(B_(-1)x,y) + mu_n(Px,B_(-1)y). This is the beta-mode-zero specialization of the actual signed Borcherds identity. Both parity projections and reverse terms are retained before the zero-binomial sums collapse. No homogeneous-input assumption is used."))), DescribeRole.Theorem),
            Describe.Lean(DescribeId.Create("latticebrstcurrentidentities-even-zero-mode"),
                DeclarationHandle.Create("D5/S3/VertexAlgebra/Lattice/PhysicalLie/LatticeBRSTCurrentIdentities.even_zero_mode"),
                H("The even zero-mode commutator as a vector identity"), StatementSource.WithoutFormula(), AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(),
                Blocks(Paragraph(Text("For every D, states u,v,w and integer n, if Pu = u and Pv = v, then mu_0(u,mu_n(v,w)) = mu_n(mu_0(u,v),w) + mu_n(v,mu_0(u,w)). The third state is unrestricted. The actual homogeneous Borcherds identity, at even parities and zero binomial index, proves this on the original carrier."))), DescribeRole.Theorem),
            Describe.Lean(DescribeId.Create("latticebrstcurrentidentities-current-leftleibniz"),
                DeclarationHandle.Create("D5/S3/VertexAlgebra/Lattice/PhysicalLie/LatticeBRSTCurrentIdentities.current_leftLeibniz"),
                H("Exact unsigned current Leibniz before quotienting"), StatementSource.WithoutFormula(), AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(),
                Blocks(Paragraph(Text("For every D and x,y,z : State D with Px = -x and Py = -y, K(x,K(y,z)) = K(K(x,y),z) + K(y,K(x,z)). The third state z is arbitrary. Oddness makes B_(-1)x and B_(-1)y even; b_minus_one_mode, b_square and even_zero_mode identify the nested currents as literal vectors. No cycle, quotient, inverse-Gram, energy or rank assumption occurs."))), DescribeRole.Theorem),
            Paragraph(Text("For D : LatticeData and H : Matrix (Fin D.rank) (Fin D.rank) Complex, assume hHG : H * gramComplex D = 1 and hGH : gramComplex D * H = 1. Let x,y : cycles D H = ker(totalCharge D H), with hx : B_0 x = 0 and hy : B_0 y = 0. With Q = totalCharge D H, B_j = ghostB D j, P = the original parity, K(x,y) = originalMode D 0 (B_(-1)x) y and L_0 = totalL0 D H, the application is L_0(K(x,y)) = 0. The original total_ward_b D H 0, evaluated at K(x,y), gives Q(B_0 K(x,y)) + B_0(Q(K(x,y))) = L_0(K(x,y)). The existing current_cycle D H hHG hGH x y gives Q(K(x,y)) = 0: its current_charge identity is Q(K(x,y)) = -K(Qx,y) - K(Px,Qy), and Qx = Qy = 0 because x,y are cycles. The retained current_b0 D x y hx hy gives B_0 K(x,y) = 0, using the original tensor antighost CAR to move B_0 through B_(-1) and the beta-mode-one Borcherds identity with the vanishing B_(-1) square. Linearity therefore reduces the Ward left side to Q(0) + B_0(0) = 0. This application keeps arbitrary original lattice charges and the original epsilon conventions; it assumes no rank-26, number-one, homogeneous-parity, zero-input-energy, positivity, nonzero-momentum or real/integral inverse-Gram condition. It remains ordinary exposition from the original Ward and current suppliers, without a separate named theorem.")),
            Paragraph(Text("The tensor CAR and native Borcherds suppliers retain their original lattice and ghost attribution, Scott Carnahan's residue calculus, and Mathlib. These are algebraic current identities on the stated complex; no literature novelty, physical positivity, no-ghost theorem, complete string theory, spacetime reconstruction or AdS/CFT conclusion is asserted.")),
            Paragraph(Text("Direct mathematical suppliers: "), Ref("D5/S3/VertexAlgebra/Lattice/LatticeBRSTCohomologyBVSecondOrder")))));
